window.__finlexDocLoaded(10212,{"id":10212,"articles":[{"id":1000885,"no":"Overview","heading":"Scope & Core Objective (Public Summary)","text":"Identifies three narrow classes of freestanding financial instruments (mandatorily redeemable shares, repurchase obligations, and certain share-settled obligations with predominantly fixed monetary value) that MUST be classified as liabilities, supplemented by ASC 815-40 and SEC temporary equity (mezzanine) rules.","seq":0},{"id":1000886,"no":"ASC 480-10-25","heading":"Three Mandatory Liability Classes for Freestanding Instruments","text":"ASC 480-10 requires classifying THREE specific classes of freestanding financial instruments as LIABILITIES (rather than equity):\n• (1) Mandatorily Redeemable Financial Instruments (25-4): Shares embodying an unconditional obligation requiring the issuer to redeem them by transferring assets at a specified/determinable date or upon an event CERTAIN to occur (e.g., death of holder).\n• (2) Obligations to Repurchase Issuer's Equity Shares by Transferring Assets (25-8): e.g., written put options or forward purchase contracts on own shares settled physically or net in cash.\n• (3) Certain Obligations to Issue a Variable Number of Shares (25-14): Obligations whose monetary value at inception is based solely or predominantly on (a) a fixed monetary amount known at inception (e.g., 'settle $10M in shares'), (b) variations in something other than the issuer's equity fair value, or (c) variations inversely related to the issuer's share price.","seq":1},{"id":1000887,"no":"ASC 480-10-S99-3A","heading":"SEC Temporary / Mezzanine Equity & Interaction with ASC 815-40","text":"• SEC Temporary / Mezzanine Equity (ASC 480-10-S99-3A / ASR 268): For SEC registrants, redeemable equity securities whose redemption is OUTSIDE THE SOLE CONTROL of the issuer (e.g., VC/PE convertible preferred stock redeemable upon a deemed liquidation / change of control, or puttable at holder's option after 5 years) CANNOT be presented in permanent stockholders' equity — they are presented between Total Liabilities and Stockholders' Equity as 'Temporary / Mezzanine Equity'.\n• Accretion to Redemption Value: If redemption is probable (or currently redeemable), accrete carrying amount to redemption value through retained earnings/APIC (impacting EPS via numerator adjustment, NOT net income).\n• Freestanding Warrants & Conversion Features: Instruments outside ASC 480 are next tested under ASC 815-40 (2-step indexation & equity-classification test) to determine equity vs. derivative liability.","seq":2},{"id":1000888,"no":"ASC 480 vs IAS 32 / CAS 37","heading":"Key Cross-Framework Divergences (Mezzanine Equity vs. IAS 32 Liability)","text":"• Conditionally Redeemable Preferred Stock (Huge Impact on Pre-IPO / Tech Companies): Under IAS 32 / CAS 37, preferred shares with redemption triggers outside the issuer's sole control are generally FINANCIAL LIABILITIES (often measured at FVTPL, creating massive P&L fair-value losses as company valuation rises!); under US GAAP (ASC 480 + SEC S99-3A), they sit in Temporary/Mezzanine Equity with ZERO net income fair-value volatility.\n• Fixed-for-Fixed vs. Indexation: IAS 32 applies a strict 'fixed-for-fixed' rule for equity derivatives; US GAAP applies ASC 815-40's two-step indexation and settlement framework.","seq":3},{"id":1000889,"no":"Official Access","heading":"Official FASB Codification & Reference Entry","text":"Official Portal (FASB Accounting Standards Codification®): https://asc.fasb.org/\nStatus: in_force (FASB ASC free Basic View available at https://asc.fasb.org/).","seq":4}]});
